{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>But if, etc.</b> The sense: if you listen, you shall eat; and if you rebel, you shall eat the eating of the sword. Or a bet may be missing, as in \"the found, the house of YHWH\" <small>(2 Kings 18:16)</small>." "And this is the truth, <b>for the mouth of YHWH has spoken</b>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes 2 Kings 18:16 where the standard text reads כִּי־נִמְצְאוּ בֵּית־יְהוָה, apparently suggesting that the bet should be understood as present in בֵּית־יְהוָה ('house of YHWH'). The phrase 'הנמצא' is rendered hyper-literally; the reference to 2 Kings 18:16 confirms the citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:04.129094050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}